#: Advanced.md:477
msgid "Appendix"
msgstr ""

#: Advanced.md:478
msgid "Arena"
msgstr ""

#: Advanced.md:479
msgid ""
"The `sharedArena` class copies the idea of the _arena allocator_ to assign "
"the shared memory data to specific types. The class is made up to not "
"overlap the suballocation on each other."
msgstr ""

#: Advanced.md:495
msgid ""
"Here the \"arena\" concept is used on a chunk of memory that is already "
"allocatea and that will automatically be deallocated after the kernel has "
"finished its job. We are just using a toy version of the tecnique to treat "
"subsequent chunks of \"generically\" allocated memory as if it of a certain "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: Advanced.md:497
msgid ""
"The standard Arena allocator tecnique is more complex and aims at managing "
"the memory with minimizing the number of `malloc` and `free` used. In a few "
"words you allocate a big chunk of memory once and then you manage it by "
"assigning part of it to different array or other structures, then the point "
"become that you can reutilize the already allocated memory without asking "
"for new allocation or deallocation. You just need to apply some more care in"
" what you are asking doing with the initialization of the date and "
"expecially in avoinding the reutilization of old pointers."
msgstr ""
